<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#bronze-working">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bronze-working</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bronze-working is the craft of producing tools, weapons and ornaments from bronze, an alloy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, with access to metal resources of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a>, developed an important metalworking tradition. It formed part of the economy and trade of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>.</p></div>
